      "worked": "Opposite sides of a parallelogram have equal coordinate changes. Consider each choice of the given vertex opposite the fourth vertex $D$.\n\nIf $D$ is opposite $A$:\n$$\\begin{align*}D&=(-1+0-1,\\ 2+3-1)\\\\D&=(-2,4)\\end{align*}$$\nIf $D$ is opposite $B$:\n$$\\begin{align*}D&=(1+0-(-1),\\ 1+3-2)\\\\D&=(2,2)\\end{align*}$$\nIf $D$ is opposite $C$:\n$$\\begin{align*}D&=(1+(-1)-0,\\ 1+2-3)\\\\D&=(0,0)\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
